  "deltaAssessment": [
    "Only lab.py and test_request_window.py differ from the37source V2snapshot. Controller now holds the existing request_condition for its complete shutdown/detach/native-close sequence and skips a request if an actually finished worker already removed that exact owned object.",
    "Server.shutdown_request serializes normal worker shutdown/close under the same condition. Its default RLock preserves reentrant admission rejection. Worker and controller native-close sequences cannot now overlap while CPython releases the GIL; actual worker finally still performs completion accounting. This closes the sole previously reported P2.",
    "The sixth regression uses real HTTP threads: controller shutdown pauses while holding the lock; handler actually receives a byte and finishes; worker attempts normal teardown but cannot reach tracked native shutdown until controller releases ownership. Event observations and eventual admitted==finished/active0 distinguish exclusion from a merely absent worker.",
    "Collector seal, immutable controller request-window write, matrix/fresh-revocation requires and accepted V2 semantic boundaries are unchanged. These close only request intervals, not all media backings."
  ],
